 ahead by double digits", "Fragmented opposition: an independent (Bodnar) and Libertarian draw votes away from Democrat Bankhead", "All ten expert ratings rate the race Safe or Solid or Likely R; markets price Democratic chances near 1%"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Republican Kurt Alme leading by 20 or more points, the state leans heavily Republican, and the anti-GOP vote is split between an independent and a Libertarian. Markets and all ten expert ratings agree the race is effectively decided, so the forecast sits near the polling average rather than the milder fundamentals-only estimate.", "watch": "A sharp consolidation of Democratic, independent, and Libertarian voters behind one non-Republican candidate could narrow the margin, though it would still be unlikely to flip the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Steve Daines (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Montana's open Senate seat, left vacant by Steve Daines's retirement, is expected to stay in Republican hands. Republican Kurt Alme has led every published poll, most recently by about 21 points, while Democrat Alani Bankhead runs third in some surveys behind independent Seth Bodnar, whose campaign has drawn more money and a Planned Parenthood endorsement. A Libertarian on the ballot adds further vote-splitting on the non-Republican side.\n\nAlme also holds a large fundraising edge over Bankhead, though outside groups have spent heavily on both sides. All ten expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one percent chance. The main open question is the size of the winning margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -15.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0028, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.004, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0021, "margin": -20.0}, {"date